      "body": "## Purpose\n\nFixes #46131.\n\n#43032 enabled per-workitem GQA for decode workitems in mixed batches. However, the executor used scheduler workitem token counts (`q_token_num == 1`) to decide whether a workitem was decode. With split-KV enabled, prefill requests can be partitioned into single-token workitems, so those prefill tiles could incorrectly take the mixed-batch GQA path.\n\nThis PR makes mixed-batch GQA decisions use the original request query length from `query_start_loc` instead of the partitioned workitem length, in both the attention and reduction paths. It also keeps the GQA tile size within `MaxQTileIterNum` after applying the current q-per-kv grouping so the static `first_iter_flag` array invariant holds for non-divisible GQA ratios.\n\nDuplicate-work check: I checked the issue comments and open PRs for `46131`, `mixed batch GQA CPU attention`, and `cpu attn gqa decode workitem`; no open PR currently addresses this issue.\n\nAI assistance was used to investigate and prepare this change.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- `git diff --check -- csrc/cpu/cpu_attn_impl.hpp tests/kernels/attention/test_cpu_attn.py`\n- `uv run --no-project python -m compileall -q tests/kernels/attention/test_cpu_attn.py`\n- Intended CPU kernel regression test: `python -m pytest tests/kernels/attention/test_cpu_attn.py::test_varlen_with_paged_kv_mixed_gqa_prefill_split_vec -q`\n\n## Test Result\n\n- `git diff --check -- csrc/cpu/cpu_attn_impl.hpp tests/kernels/attention/test_cpu_attn.py`: passed\n- `uv run --no-project python -m compileall -q tests/kernels/attention/test_cpu_attn.py`: passed\n- Target pytest could not be completed in my local WSL environment because it does not have torch 2.11+cpu and a compiled vLLM CPU extension installed. The new regression test is added for CPU CI coverage.\n\n---\n<details>\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\n- [x] The test plan, such as providing test command.\n- [x] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\n</details>",
      "changedFiles": 2,
